-- #62.  The MULTI-LINE removed-record forms, which the first cut of the
-- shape-keyed scan silently stopped diagnosing (it stopped its walk at the
-- `TIndent` between `=` and `{`).  This is the population that matters most:
-- `docs/spec/language-design.md` still documents the brace-less form below as
-- THE product-type syntax, so it is what a migrating reader types.
--
-- Both forms lex as ONE logical line — `Person` `canEndExpr`, so a deeper line
-- is absorbed as an application continuation.  Only the first is reported
-- (the pre-scan returns the FIRST match); the sibling record_decl_removed.mdk
-- covers the single-line form and the export-modifier form is covered by the
-- probe recorded in the safety comment.
record Person
  name : String
  age : Int

main = println 1
